WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.413
The children quickly realized that the strange man at the door was Eliza's fiancé.

2
00:00:06.414 --> 00:00:11.052
And that an invisible Eliza was holding his hand tightly.

3
00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:16.108
"He keeps saying he can't see me," said Eliza's voice.

4
00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:21.009
"Well, I can't," protested her fiancé.

5
00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:29.447
"I know you have the ring," Gerald whispered to Eliza. "Go inside."

6
00:00:29.448 --> 00:00:30.664
"What's going on?"

7
00:00:30.665 --> 00:00:34.615
asked the man, who seemed to relax once Eliza released him.

8
00:00:34.616 --> 00:00:37.597
"Have I been acting strange?"

9
00:00:37.598 --> 00:00:41.632
"Very strange," said Mabel.

10
00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:45.392
"You should go home and lie down," said Gerald.

11
00:00:45.393 --> 00:00:48.123
"The sun is very hot today."

12
00:00:48.124 --> 00:00:52.995
"Yes . . . yes . . . ," the man said with a puzzled look.

13
00:00:52.996 --> 00:00:54.753
"I'll do that."

14
00:00:54.754 --> 00:01:00.101
Once he was gone, the children went inside to talk to Eliza.

15
00:01:00.102 --> 00:01:04.086
It took a while to convince her that she really was invisible.

16
00:01:04.087 --> 00:01:08.886
She said she'd found the ring in the bed and "borrowed" it.

17
00:01:08.887 --> 00:01:12.183
"Do I have to stay like this?" she wailed.

18
00:01:12.184 --> 00:01:15.869
"No man will marry a girl he can't see."

19
00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:20.157
"It doesn't last forever," said Mabel kindly.

20
00:01:20.158 --> 00:01:23.721
"And we'll help you," added Kathleen.

21
00:01:23.722 --> 00:01:28.428
"Now let's get Mademoiselle's tea ready," said Gerald.

22
00:01:28.429 --> 00:01:31.462
"And ours!" said Jimmy.

23
00:01:31.463 --> 00:01:34.778
"No." Gerald looked thoughtful.

24
00:01:34.779 --> 00:01:37.073
"We'll have a picnic and take Eliza.

25
00:01:37.074 --> 00:01:42.864
I'll go get some cakes."

26
00:01:42.865 --> 00:01:48.322
While Gerald was out, Mademoiselle came home from visiting the castle.

27
00:01:48.323 --> 00:01:51.857
She seemed tired and a little sad.

28
00:01:51.858 --> 00:01:57.073
As soon as Gerald returned, the children and Eliza started for the castle.

29
00:01:57.074 --> 00:02:01.779
They watched the sun go down as they had their picnic on the castle grounds.

30
00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:05.441
"I should go home now," said Mabel.

31
00:02:05.442 --> 00:02:10.233
"Well, I can't go home like this," said Eliza.

32
00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:13.200
She pointed to a white marble temple.

33
00:02:13.201 --> 00:02:18.056
"I'd live in that little white house over there if it had any walls."

34
00:02:18.057 --> 00:02:22.875
"Oh, you mean the Temple of Apollo," said Mabel.

35
00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:27.881
"What a lot of steps to clean!" said Eliza. "Why

36
00:02:27.882 --> 00:02:30.560
do they make houses without walls? Who'd

37
00:02:30.561 --> 00:02:36.412
live in . . ." She paused. "What's that?" "What?"

38
00:02:36.413 --> 00:02:39.808
asked Kathleen and Jimmy together. They

39
00:02:39.809 --> 00:02:41.946
couldn't see anything. "That

40
00:02:41.947 --> 00:02:48.001
white thing coming down the steps," said Eliza. "Oh!

41
00:02:48.002 --> 00:02:50.365
It's a young man. But

42
00:02:50.366 --> 00:02:53.727
he looks like a statue." "I

43
00:02:53.728 --> 00:02:59.302
thought I saw the statues come alive last night!" exclaimed Gerald. "I

44
00:02:59.303 --> 00:03:02.051
think it happens after sunset." "

45
00:03:02.052 --> 00:03:05.696
I never saw them come alive," said Mabel.

46
00:03:05.697 --> 00:03:08.873
"And I've often been in the gardens at night."

47
00:03:08.874 --> 00:03:13.246
"I know I saw them moving," said Gerald.

48
00:03:13.247 --> 00:03:16.644
"I believe you," said Mabel.

49
00:03:16.645 --> 00:03:22.120
"I wonder if you can only see them move when you're invisible."

50
00:03:22.121 --> 00:03:25.702
"You're probably right," Gerald replied.

51
00:03:25.703 --> 00:03:31.054
"Oh look!" said Eliza. "There's another statue!

52
00:03:31.055 --> 00:03:34.380
He's got little wings on his feet!"

53
00:03:34.381 --> 00:03:39.530
"That's probably Hermes, the messenger of the gods," said Gerald.

54
00:03:39.531 --> 00:03:43.096
"What are you talking about?" asked Jimmy.

55
00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:46.011
"I don't see any moving statues."

56
00:03:46.012 --> 00:03:49.495
The gardens stretched in front of the children.

57
00:03:49.496 --> 00:03:52.665
They could only see the statues standing still.

58
00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:58.053
But Eliza could see statues walking over the lawn and swimming in the lake.

59
00:03:58.054 --> 00:04:04.551
"Oh, here's a dear little boy," she said.

60
00:04:04.552 --> 00:04:07.424
"He's coming right toward me."

61
00:04:07.425 --> 00:04:13.149
The next moment she was screaming.

62
00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.936
There was the sound of boots on gravel—Eliza was running away!

63
00:04:17.937 --> 00:04:22.112
"She must have touched the statue!" cried Gerald.

64
00:04:22.113 --> 00:04:26.915
"Then she became afraid, just like I did last night.

65
00:04:26.916 --> 00:04:31.095
Come on," he added.

66
00:04:31.096 --> 00:04:35.363
"We have to catch her before she frightens everybody in town with her screams."

67
00:04:35.364 --> 00:04:41.472
Mabel stayed at the castle, but the others ran as fast as they could.

68
00:04:41.473 --> 00:04:45.239
They didn't catch up with Eliza until they reached their own back door.

69
00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:51.910
Just as the church clock struck the half-hour, Eliza suddenly reappeared.

70
00:04:51.911 --> 00:04:55.291
She held out her hand.

71
00:04:55.292 --> 00:05:01.832
The magic ring was on her finger.

